<title>HONG KONG: Dickson Cons interim net rises sharply.</title>
<headline>Dickson Cons interim net rises sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   8.24	 vs 0.1</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  22.50 gain vs 1.64 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    25.30	vs 0.36</p>
<p>    Turnover		     309.83     vs 246.08</p>
<p>    Company name		 Dickson Construction</p>
<p>				     International Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Dickson Construction engages in construction and civil engineering in Hong Kong, specialising in public sector building projects.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$30.87 million on repurchases of convertible bonds, HK$1.64 million exchange gain on translation of convertible bonds and HK$10 million loss on provision for trade debtors.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
